{
  "_guidelines": {
    "action_items": "A task someone is expected to do after the meeting. Owner = person who committed, was named, or accepted the request; 'Unassigned' if nobody did (offers such as 'no promises' do not count). Deadline = resolved ISO date of the final due date, null if none or only vague timing. Relative dates follow the documented convention ('next <weekday>' = that weekday in the following calendar week). Scheduling the next meeting is not labelled as an action unless someone is assigned to do it.",
    "decisions": "Outcomes the group settled on. confirmed = settled; tentative = provisional, conditional or deferred ('for now', 'if ... then', 'hold off until'); rejected = an option explicitly turned down. Suggestions and questions are not decisions.",
    "risks": "Problems, risks, concerns or blockers raised as current or future issues (not past incidents being reported as history). blocker = work cannot proceed until something happens.",
    "questions": "Questions or issues still open at the end of the meeting: unanswered, deferred, or explicitly unresolved.",
    "evidence": "Each label lists one or more distinctive substrings; a prediction matches if any of its evidence sentences contains one of them (case-insensitive). Each gold item can be matched once.",
    "split": "dev_* files were used while developing the rules. test_* files were written and labelled before their first evaluation (frozen in RESULTS_heldout_v1.md); error analysis on them then led to further changes, so later test numbers are post-hoc. holdout2_* files were written and labelled after those changes and evaluated once.",
    "deadline_lists": "A deadline given as a list accepts any of the listed dates (used where the transcript supports two readings)."
  },
